.DS_Store
*.zip
*.crx
*.pem
node_modules/
CLAUDE.md

# Local agent / editor state — this repo is public.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
.env
.env.*

# Local dev tooling, same rule as store/'s build scripts: this repo is public,
# and a canary that drives a browser against YouTube is working material, not
# product. Carries its own node_modules, a Chrome profile and failure
# screenshots, none of which belong in a repo whose whole pitch is that the
# extension is readable end to end in ten minutes.
tools/

# SEO/AEO strategy, target queries, channel plans and outreach drafts. Working
# material by definition, and the outreach drafts in particular stop working the
# moment they are public — a reply template anyone can read is not a reply.
seo/

# store/ is the publishing workspace, and most of it is working material in the
# same sense CLAUDE.md is: listing copy, the launch plan, the asset generator
# and the build script. Two things in it are load-bearing on the public side
# and stay tracked:
#
#   PRIVACY.md — this exact path is the privacy policy URL registered on the
#                live Chrome Web Store listing. A 404 there is a required field
#                gone missing, not a broken link.
#   assets/    — the README renders its screenshots and donation QR codes from
#                here. (docs/ keeps its own copies, so the landing page does
#                not depend on this.)
#
# Ordering matters: store/* has to exclude entries individually, or git will
# not descend into store/assets/ to see the re-include below it.
store/*
!store/PRIVACY.md
!store/assets/
